course: dictionary
lesson: 2647
title: Detergent: a word for cleaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A detergent is a liquid or powder that helps you clean, especially when washing clothes or dishes. Context tells you this: «Washing powder contains detergents and enzymes that break down fat stains.» The clues are washing and stains, so a detergent must be something that cleans.
explain: Some sentences warn you about danger, and the words show it. «Never try online challenges with detergent pods; they have hurt and killed children.» The words never, hurt and killed are the clues. A detergent pod is not a sweet, even when it looks like one.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Soap and detergent do the cleaning, not the foam.» Put "cleaning liquid" in place of detergent and it still makes sense. That tells you your meaning is right.
fact: A detergent is a liquid or powder used for cleaning, especially clothes and dishes.
fact: «Laundry detergent» means detergent for washing clothes, and «washing-up liquid» is a detergent for dishes.
fact: Detergent breaks up grease, which is why it is used in science lessons.
fact: «Detergent pods» look like sweets but are poisonous, so they must be kept locked away from little children.
fact: Never swallow detergent. If someone does, tell a grown-up and get help at once.
exercise: «Washing powder contains detergents and enzymes that break down fat stains.» What is a detergent? | *Something used for cleaning, like washing powder | A type of food for small children | A bubble that floats in the air
exercise: «Detergent pods ... look like sweets but are poisonous.» Why are they kept locked away? | *Because they can poison little children | Because they are too expensive to waste | Because they taste too sour
exercise: Which of these is a detergent? | A paper towel | A cold drink | *Washing-up liquid
test: Why must «detergent pods» be kept away from little children? | They make the room smell nice | *They are poisonous and look like sweets | They are too heavy to lift
test: In «a drop of detergent», what does detergent mean? | A kind of sweet | A soft toy for babies | *A liquid used for cleaning
exam: Which word in «they have hurt and killed children» shows that detergent pods are dangerous? | challenges | online | *killed | pods
